    "type": "message",
    "user": "U039XR2B72A",
    "text": "No, handling interrupts of course does not require resetting the device. This is more of a hard-reset procedure if you somehow ended up in a device state. However:\n• if your driver doesn't have serious bugs it should not happen\n• your driver does not have to handle device bugs (there could be some regardless how well the device is tested)\n• since the device is emulated in Qemu, a less error-prone approach is just restarting qemu each time you compile a new driver version",
