    "user": "U08EXEABDFX",
    "text": "I am confused regarding the value of `fence_value`. It seems tests are interchanchably using `fence_value=0` in `ioct_wait` to either wait forever (`invalid_cmd` test) or to not wait at all (`run_bad_descriptor`).\n\nMore context: `invalid_cmd` calls `do_run_and_wait_with_err` which calls  `do_wait_for_err(fd, fence_value: 0)` . I guess here the idea is to wait for the error. However, in `run_bad_descriptor` there is `do_wait(fd, fence_value: 0)` after a valid `run`, here I don't really understand what is the point of the `do_wait`, since it definitly doesn't wait for anything to finish, nor for any errors.",
