  {
    "client_msg_id": "7b5ff361-84f6-41a0-88e7-ee6fed56ab4d",
    "type": "message",
    "user": "U039XR2B72A",
    "text": "Ok, so in `run_bad_descriptor` the `do_wait(fd, 0)` is somewhat unnecessary - this only tests that waiting does not fail and finishes immediately since the fence counter is already 0 or larger at the beginning.\nIn `invalid_cmd` the idea is that the waiting should be infinite but an error should wake it up. So this test actually has a bug which for some reason didn't occur with my solution - probably the device manages to process some commands before my driver gets to the waiting because calling wait if an error occurred before the wait call should also fail the wait. \n\nI will fix it later.",
    "ts": "1747286907.775099",
    "thread_ts": "1747252780.178309",
